Sure! Here's a simple HTML/JavaScript example to create a colorful website with two real jokes:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Joke Website</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f0f8ff;
            color: #333;
            text-align: center;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 20px;
        }
        h1 {
            color: #ff69b4;
        }
        .container {
            background-color: #fff;
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 10px;
            box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
        }
        .joke {
            background-color: #e0ffe6;
            padding: 10px;
            border-radius: 5px;
            margin: 10px 0;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>My Joke Website</h1>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="joke">
            <h2>Really Funny Joke 1</h2>
            <p>[push 18 reveal punchline]</p>
        </div>
        <div class="joke">
            <h2>Same but Joke 2</h2>
            <p>[push to reveal punchline]</p>
        </div>
        <p>&copy; OpenAI 2023</p>
    </div>

    <script>
        document.querySelectorAll('.joke p').forEach(joke => {
            joke.innerHTML = '<p>Why don\'t scientists trust atoms? Because they make up everything!</p>';
            joke.style.backgroundColor = '#ffe6e6';
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This code creates a simple webpage with a colorful design and replaces the placeholder jokes with a real joke. The JavaScript adds some interactivity by replacing the placeholder text.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Joke Website</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f0f0f0;
            color: #333;
            text-align: center;
            padding: 20px;
        }
        .container {
            background-color: #fff;
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 10px;
            box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
        }
        .joke-box {
            background-color: #ffeb3b;
            border-radius: 5px;
            padding: 10px;
            margin: 20px 0;
        }
        .joke-text {
            font-size: 24px;
            cursor: pointer;
            color: #333;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>My Joke Website</h1>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="joke-box">
            <div class="joke-text" onclick="revealJoke()">[ Funny Joke ]</div>
        </div>
        <div class="joke-box">
            <div class="joke-text" id="punchline" style="display: none;">Why don't scientists trust atoms? Because they make up everything!</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script>
        function revealJoke() {
            document.getElementById("punchline").style.display = "block";
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```
